Add a setting for the shadow of menus and tooltips

QtCurve gives a drop shadow to a menu, a tooltip and a combo box list.
The Qt styles also give one to a detached tool bar and a detached dock
widget. No setting switches that shadow off. A user whose window
manager draws its own shadow gets two shadows on one menu.

The Options struct now carries popupShadow, and each parser reads the
stylerc key of the same name. No code reads the field yet, so this
change alters no behaviour.

The default is true, which keeps the shadow that users have today. An
absent key falls back to the built-in default, so a configuration file
from an earlier release needs no migration clause.

All four toolkit trees take the member, the read and the default. A
tree without the member ignores a key that the user set, which splits
the behaviour between two toolkits of one desktop. The three Qt trees
also take a write line. The GTK 2 tree takes none, because it has no
write path.

The change sits on the branch work/popup-shadow of the local tree, as
the first commit. The fork wyn/qtcurve holds that branch. Merge request
!19 on system/qtcurve holds that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

